import ../../../testing/driver.dl
window queued tabs:
    ribbon "Tabs" at 0 0 sized 600 by 168:
        tab "A":
            ribbon group "First":
                tool "One" with icon "copy"
        tab "B":
            ribbon group "Second":
                tool "Two" with icon "paste"
        tab "C":
            ribbon group "Third":
                tool "Three" with icon "cut"

document changing controls:
    button "Earlier"
    text surface "Source" containing "abc" using no UI appearance
    button "Later"
set state to 0
set instance to an instance of queued tabs with state (the address of state)
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 800 by 480 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 258 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
set index to 0
loop while index < 4:
    queue UI input of kind 3 key 262 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
    queue UI input of kind 6 key 262 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
    increment index
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((the value of "Tabs" in (the address of instance)) = 1) reporting "Queued arrows used focus from the previous paint"
require condition (view's focused's node's text = "B") reporting "Focus did not follow the selected tab"
queue UI input of kind 3 key 258 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 257 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((the value of "Tabs" in (the address of instance)) = 2) reporting "Queued Tab/Enter activated the previous control"
queue UI input of kind 3 key 258 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 1 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (view's focused's node's text = "B") reporting "Shift-Tab did not move focus backward"
close the address of view
close the address of instance

set instance to an instance of changing controls
set window to the address of instance
set earlier to the control labeled "Earlier" in window
set source to the control labeled "Source" in window
set later to the control labeled "Later" in window
set UI control earlier enabled false in window
set view to a UI view of window sized 600 by 400 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set editor to the UI layout for element source in (view's layout)
activate UI layout editor in (the address of view)
set view's selection's anchor and view's selection's caret to 1
set UI control earlier enabled true in window
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((view's focused = editor) and (view's text focus = source)) reporting "Enabling an earlier control changed the focused editor."
require condition (view's selection's caret = 1) reporting "A focus-list update replaced the editor's selection."
set UI control earlier enabled false in window
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (view's focused = editor) reporting "Disabling an earlier control changed the focused editor."
set UI control source read only true in window
queue UI input of kind 3 key 258 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
process UI input in (the address of view)
require condition (view's focused's node = later) reporting "Preserving focus identity overrode explicit Tab navigation."
queue UI input of kind 3 key 258 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 1 containing "" in (the address of view)
process UI input in (the address of view)
require condition (view's focused = editor) reporting "Preserving focus identity overrode explicit Shift-Tab navigation."
set UI control source enabled false in window
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (view's focused's node = later) reporting "A disabled focused control remained in the focus list."
set UI control earlier enabled true in window
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (view's focused's node = later) reporting "A later control lost focus when the list grew."
close the address of view
close window
print line "Keyboard focus updates between queued events without a paint."
